# ASSAULT BIKE INTERVALS

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Assault Bike Intervals are repeated maximal or near-maximal efforts performed on an air-resistance bike to develop anaerobic power, aerobic recovery and whole-body work capacity.

Within CAS, they are considered one of the most effective low-impact conditioning methods for combat athletes.

---

# Philosophy

Combat athletes need conditioning that improves performance without unnecessarily increasing orthopedic stress.

The Assault Bike delivers maximal metabolic stimulus while preserving the joints.

CAS frequently selects this modality during periods of high technical or strength training volume.

